[center][size=6][b]RaceMenu Together[/b][/size]
[size=4]RaceMenu Appearance Sync for Skyrim Together Reborn[/size][/center]

Your friends see the character you made. Everything you set up in [b]RaceMenu[/b] - sculpting, sliders, body morphs, height and bone scales, tattoos and makeup, a preset you loaded - shows on your character on every screen in your [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] session, instead of the plain vanilla face and body.

[size=5][b]Features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Your whole RaceMenu appearance is shared[/b]: sculpting (including imported heads), RaceMenu's sliders, body morphs, node transforms, overlays and the rest of a RaceMenu preset.
[*][b]Custom races and bodies[/b]: body morphs from custom races such as UBE come along, as long as everyone has the same body installed.
[*][b]Always up to date[/b]: your appearance is sent when you join, every time you close RaceMenu, and again whenever someone else joins.
[*][b]Holds up against NPC body mods[/b]: BodyGen and OBody treat other players' characters like NPCs and give them random bodies; RaceMenu Together puts the owner's body back.
[*][b]Works with the official Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.3[/b] from Nexus: the main file (Skyrim [b]1.7.104[/b]) and the optional file for [b]1.6.1170 / 1.6.1179[/b].
[*][b]Also works with Skyrim Together Reborn 1.8.5[/b] (absol89), including its [b]1.5.97[/b] port.
[*][b]No server changes[/b]: it plays on any regular server of your Skyrim Together version.
[*][b]Plays nicely with SkyParkour Together[/b]: our mods share one launcher, so you can run them together.
[*][b]RaceMenu itself is untouched[/b]: this mod contains no RaceMenu files; it uses RaceMenu's own preset functions.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[b]Every player in the session[/b] needs all of these:
[list]
[*]Skyrim Special/Anniversary Edition [b]1.5.97, 1.6.1170, 1.6.1179 or 1.7.104[/b]
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] for your game version
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/19080]RaceMenu[/url] for your game version (not included)
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/69993]Skyrim Together Reborn[/url] [b]1.8.3[/b] (the Nexus main or optional file for your game version), or Skyrim Together Reborn [b]1.8.5[/b]
[*][b]The same appearance mods as the other players.[/b] A preset only names meshes, textures, hair and morphs. If a friend uses UBE, a hair mod, a skin or BodySlide morphs, you need that mod too (and your body built in BodySlide with [i]Build Morphs[/i] ticked) to see it.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Which Skyrim Together do I have?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]1.8.3 (official)[/b]: you downloaded Skyrim Together Reborn from its Nexus page. Main file = Skyrim 1.7.104; optional file "for 1.6.1170" = Skyrim 1.6.1170/1.6.1179. [b]Not sure? This is you.[/b]
[*][b]1.8.5[/b]: you use absol89's 1.8.5 build, or play on Skyrim 1.5.97 with the 1.5.97 port.
[/list]
1.8.3 and 1.8.5 can't join each other's servers, so everyone in your session needs the same one.

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]
Skyrim Together only starts when its launcher sits in the same folder as the rest of Skyrim Together ([font=Courier New]libcef.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]EarlyLoad.dll[/font], the UI...). How you get this mod's launcher there depends on your mod manager.
[list=1]
[*]Install Skyrim Together Reborn and RaceMenu as usual.
[*]Install this mod. The installer asks which Skyrim Together you use, then your game version.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Mod Organizer 2[/b][/size]
MO2 starts a launcher from its real folder on disk, so mod order is not enough. Copy the launcher once:
[list=1]
[*]Right-click [b]RaceMenu Together[/b] > [i]Open in Explorer[/i] and open its [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn[/font] folder.
[*]Right-click your [b]Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] mod > [i]Open in Explorer[/i] and open its [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn[/font] folder.
[*]In the Skyrim Together folder, rename [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] to [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.original.exe[/font] (your backup).
[*]Copy [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] from the RaceMenu Together folder into the Skyrim Together folder. On [b]1.5.97[/b], also copy [font=Courier New]EarlyLoad.dll[/font], [font=Courier New]TPProcess.exe[/font] and [font=Courier New]versionlib-ae-to-se-1-5-97-0.map[/font].
[*]Keep RaceMenu Together enabled (it provides the SKSE plugin) and start the game with your usual MO2 entry for Skyrim Together, the one pointing into the Skyrim Together Reborn mod. [b]Don't[/b] point an MO2 entry at the RaceMenu Together folder: the launcher can't start from there and simply closes.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Vortex[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Set RaceMenu Together to load [b]after[/b] Skyrim Together Reborn and deploy.
[*]Start the game from [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn/SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] as you normally start Skyrim Together.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Is it working?[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]Documents/My Games/Skyrim Special Edition/SKSE/RaceMenuTogether.log[/font] says [i]"Skyrim Together add-on found"[/i] and [i]"RaceMenu found"[/i].
[*]Skyrim Together's log ([font=Courier New]SkyrimTogetherReborn/logs[/font]) contains [i]"RaceMenu Together: RaceMenu Together 1.0.0 ... found"[/i], and in a session [i]"received the appearance of player ..."[/i] and [i]"appearance revision ... applied"[/i].
[/list]
[b]The launcher closes straight away[/b] (no window, no log): it was started from a folder without the rest of Skyrim Together. In MO2, do the copy steps above.
[b]The SKSE log says the add-on was not found:[/b] the game started with a different [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font]. In MO2, check the copied launcher is the one in the Skyrim Together Reborn mod; in Vortex, check the load order.
[b]Another player's body, hair or outfit is invisible:[/b] you don't have the mod or BodySlide build they use.

[size=5][b]How it works[/b][/size]
Skyrim Together shares the vanilla face and body only. This mod has two parts:
[list]
[*][b]RaceMenuTogether.dll[/b] (SKSE plugin): switches the add-on on, tells it which body morph keys belong to BodyGen and OBody, and checks that RaceMenu answers. It reads no game memory, so one DLL works on every game version.
[*][b]SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] for your Skyrim Together and game version: that exact Skyrim Together release with our small add-ons. RaceMenu Together's exports your appearance with RaceMenu's own preset function, compresses it, sends it through Skyrim Together's existing relay, and loads it onto your character on the other players' screens with RaceMenu's own preset loader. It is the same launcher our other mods ship, so they never fight over it. Nothing else in Skyrim Together is changed. On 1.5.97 the installer also adds the files Skyrim Together needs to run on that version.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]SkyParkour Together[/b]: fully compatible. Both mods ship the identical launcher carrying both add-ons, so install them in any order and both work. Keep both up to date.
[*][b]Other mods that replace or patch SkyrimTogether.exe[/b] (other Skyrim Together forks, STRPluginMessagingAPI) conflict with this mod: only one launcher can be used.
[*]Don't combine it with other RaceMenu or body morph sync mods for Skyrim Together.
[*]BodyGen, OBody and BodySlide work alongside it.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
[b]MO2:[/b] delete the copied [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.exe[/font] from the Skyrim Together Reborn mod, rename [font=Courier New]SkyrimTogether.original.exe[/font] back, then remove this mod. [b]Vortex:[/b] remove the mod.

